# the SMK-37 Elite's pad lights (ui.c pad_lights): each pad glows in its group's colour (rhythm, echo, space, colour),
# bright while held, brighter than its glow while latched (it beats), dark asleep and back when it wakes.
# padrgbN: pad N's light as 0xRRGGBB, a number
wait 300
# at rest, a glow: pad 0 Stutter (rhythm), pad 5 Macalla (echo), pad 8 Reverb and pad 10 Freeze (space), pad 15 Crush (colour)
expect padrgb0 2034434
expect padrgb3 2034434
expect padrgb5 6677
expect padrgb7 6677
expect padrgb8 1313311
expect padrgb10 1313311
expect padrgb12 2037504
expect padrgb15 2037504
# held: bright; the others as they were; up: the glow again
pad 0 down
expect padrgb0 10434570
expect padrgb1 2034434
expect padrgb8 1313311
pad 0 up
expect padrgb0 2034434
pad 10 down
expect padrgb10 6566559
pad 10 up
expect padrgb10 1313311
# latched: over the glow, at either end of its beat, and both ends are seen; held as well: bright
press >
tappad 10
release >
expect padlatch 262144
expect padrgb10 >1313311
expect padbeat10 >2
pad 10 down
expect padrgb10 6566559
wait 600
expect padrgb10 6566559
pad 10 up
tap <
expect padlatch 0
wait 100
expect padrgb10 1313311
# asleep: dark, every one; awake: the glow again
tap GLOBE
wait 300
turn K3 1
wait 200
expect sleep 15
tap PATCH
wait 902000
expect asleep 1
expect padrgb0 0
expect padrgb5 0
expect padrgb10 0
expect padrgb15 0
press FX
wait 100
release FX
wait 100
expect asleep 0
expect padrgb0 2034434
expect padrgb15 2037504
